# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# frontend/ is a pnpm workspace (pnpm-lock.yaml + pnpm-workspace.yaml). A package-lock.json here is
# never a source of truth — it is the residue of someone running `npm install` after `npm ci` failed,
# and `npm ci` fails not on a bad lockfile but because there IS no npm lockfile. `npm install` then
# "succeeds" by resolving a fresh UNLOCKED tree, so every suite run afterwards measures dependencies
# the project does not ship. Measured: an npm tree pulled vitest 4.1.10 where the pnpm lockfile pins
# 4.1.9. Ignored so it can never be committed and mistaken for the lockfile.
# Install with: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
package-lock.json

# Finder / cloud-sync conflict copies: "pos.adapter 2.ts", "PosServiceApplication 10.class".
# These are byte-stale snapshots that keep compiling. A pre-F16 copy of pos.adapter.ts made
# `npx tsc --noEmit` report errors against code nobody had edited, which makes the typecheck
# gate useless — a real regression is indistinguishable from the noise. frontend/tsconfig.json
# excludes the same shape (with `?`, since TS globs have no character classes), and
# scripts/check-stale-jars.sh sweeps the .class equivalent.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9][0-9].*

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
.next/
.turbo/
dist/
